    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "three sides given, and an angle is to be found.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. Three known sides allow direct substitution into $\\cos C=\\dfrac{a^2+b^2-c^2}{2ab}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "three angles given, and a side is to be found.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Angles determine the shape but not the size of a triangle; a known side length is needed.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "three angles and a side given, and a side is to be found.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False for direct substitution into the taught cosine-rule forms: finding a side requires two known sides and their included angle. These givens support the sine rule.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "two sides given, and the included angle is to be found.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Two side lengths alone do not determine the included angle. The angle form requires all three side lengths.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "two sides given, and a non-included angle is to be found.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Two side lengths alone do not determine a non-included angle. Direct use of the angle form requires all three side lengths.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q1-6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "one side and two angles given, and another side is to be found.",
